    "subtitle": "Boundless Murmurs of Devotion",
    "content": "(Edhi Kaala Katelin  Mozhihal)\nIn her eyes, I'm her top, her prime,\nYet words once broken can't align.\nDreams may deceive in their nighttime flight,\nBut her smiles spark a new birthright.\nIn her gaze, my feelings unfold,\nEach glance writes poetry bold.\nI'm the parchment, her eyes is the pen,\nA love's diary from start to end.\nWe wove memories, etched in time's hold,\nThough much lost, I'm still my own mold.\nDarkness births tales yet to unfold,\nHer eyes barter for my heart's stronghold.\nA part in all lives, a forever decree,\nMemories fade, yet we still see.\nUnknown tales weave threads unknown,\nEfforts echo in lives we've sown.\nHappiness dims, pain overshadows the plain,\nBut hope lingers amidst sorrow's reign.\nWith or without, I'll wait and see,\nMy eyes, forever searching, longing for thee.\nYour voice, a spell, a word so magical,\nPlanted love blooms, hope's arrival.\nIn this world, solely for you I exist,\nMy eyes, seeking, longing, never to desist.\nA myriad of feelings in love's faint gleam,\nIn darkness, a spark, a hopeful beam.\nYou, a gift priceless, beyond compare,\nLove transforms, rare poets declare.\nYour smiles, a rebirth, a radiant view,\nEach line etched, dedicated to you.\nYou, the peace I sought, my cosmic quest,\nYour memory, my heart's eternal nest.\nYour hands, teachers of life's grand lore,\nIn your presence, life's canvas I adore.\nCherish those who give, selflessly live,\nYet yearn to be a page in someone's narrative.\nHeavy my heart with every word you say,\nHer eyes, my soul's guide, lighting the way.\nIn your sorrow, if joy you find,\nKnow, in my love, solace you'll bind.\nNot permanent in life's vast array,\nBut in my love, a steadfast stay.\nHeavy with imagined emotion's tide,\nMy love's devotion, a constant guide.\nUnwanted pages may fill life's diary,\nSilence, answering questions eerie.\nIn solitude, never truly alone I'll be,\nFor in my heart, your memory sets me free.\nIn her eyes, I'm the first, the prime,\nYet words once broken can't realign.\nDreams may deceive, but in love's sight,\nWe find our way, our guiding light.........",
